OL,3,ATate brothers to remain in US jail as
OL,4,Athey fight extradition to UK
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe brothers have been held in US
OL,7,Fcustody since their July arrest, after
OL,8,Fthe UK's Crown Prosecution Service
OL,9,F(CPS) unveiled new charges. The UK has
OL,10,Funtil 16 September to submit a full
OL,11,Fextradition request, Reuters reported.
OL,13,FThey will "continue to defend
OL,14,Fthemselves against the allegations" and
OL,15,F"engage with the appropriate legal
OL,16,Fprocesses in each jurisdiction", their
OL,17,Flawyers said.
